WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.824
Spacecraft reaches

00:00:01.635 --> 00:00:03.227
Mercury on second-ever

00:00:03.039 --> 00:00:04.041
mission to enter

00:00:03.852 --> 00:00:04.607
its orbit

00:00:05.142 --> 00:00:06.981
The BepiColombo spacecraft

00:00:06.793 --> 00:00:07.748
has arrived at

00:00:07.559 --> 00:00:08.278
Mercury

00:00:08.479 --> 00:00:09.434
only the second

00:00:09.246 --> 00:00:10.295
mission ever to

00:00:10.107 --> 00:00:11.403
enter orbit around

00:00:11.215 --> 00:00:12.748
the innermost planet

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:14.366
For researchers

00:00:14.461 --> 00:00:16.607
the €1.6bn mission

00:00:16.489 --> 00:00:17.326
is the best

00:00:17.138 --> 00:00:17.833
hope yet of

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:19.189
understanding how Mercury

00:00:19.001 --> 00:00:20.298
formed so close

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:20.840
to the sun

00:00:21.065 --> 00:00:21.689
why it has

00:00:21.501 --> 00:00:22.798
a magnetic field

00:00:22.952 --> 00:00:23.906
and what makes

00:00:23.718 --> 00:00:24.555
up the frozen

00:00:24.367 --> 00:00:25.380
ice that lurks

00:00:25.192 --> 00:00:26.064
in the planet’s

00:00:25.876 --> 00:00:27.031
permanently shadowed

00:00:26.843 --> 00:00:27.621
craters

00:00:28.142 --> 00:00:29.450
Mercury is only

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:30.618
50% larger than

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:31.184
the moon but

00:00:30.996 --> 00:00:32.021
has four times

00:00:31.833 --> 00:00:32.634
its mass

00:00:33.174 --> 00:00:34.188
Full story on

00:00:33.999 --> 00:00:34.895
the dashboard
